{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1406709-expanding-crafting-rules-to-other-endeavors-as-part-of-a-24-7-server","id":1406709,"title":"Expanding Crafting Rules to other Endeavors, as part of a 24/7 server.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-08-06T17:50:40-07:00","id":1406709,"title":"Expanding Crafting Rules to other Endeavors, as part of a 24/7 server.","content":"==Background==<br /> Running an online '24/7' roleplay server has a lot of quirks and idiosyncracies compared to a more 'traditional' campaign where players meet at a table, have sessions, and the ST arbitrates a certain amount of 'downtime' in between chapters/plot arcs. Said arbitration is so that the player who decided to play a crafter isn't suddenly sitting on a heap of healing potions and +1 masterwork bastard swords in between missions, both in terms of 'time to craft' as well as in terms of 'material components required.'<br /> <br /> With many Classic World of Darkness titles, this is further compounded by the fact there are not fancy 'gold point' costs for material components or a large list of 'prerequisite spells' akin to a 3.5 SRD, and so ST fiat is needed for more details. Compared to several other lines (Werewolf notably), Changeling has the advantage that a Treasure's 'level' and number of mythic components is equal to the 'level' of an Art being replicated within said Treasure. However, for chimerical items, the actual material costs are 'in the open' so to speak.<br /> <br /> Looking back at 2nd ed Dreams and Nightmares, the rules for crafting were more...esoteric. That is, a Chimerical Item was made out of &quot;dreamstuff&quot;, with a &quot;volume&quot; representing a nonspecific amount of Dreamstuff that could be used in order to craft an item. A Chimerical Item required a minimum of one &quot;base&quot; element and two &quot;supporting&quot; elements for a total cost of 3 Dreamstuff, with each 'rede' costing an additional base and two supporting elements...but a supporting element could be 'reused' if sympathetic to the redes in question...then the amount of 'chimerical points' a volume provided depended on if it was harvested on a given holiday (and if the harvester was Unseelie), which led to even more bookkeeping oddness...and yeah.<br /> <br /> ==Implementation==<br /> Ultimately, I decided to 'streamline' things by taking the C20 Chimerical Crafting rules and 'adapting' them, so the rules for Chimerical Crafting become a catchall for any type of extended project. This includes several details:<br /> <br /> Every project has its own dicepool for 'planning' and 'execution'.<br /> -Planning takes 40 hours instead of 8. However, every success (rather than every 5 successes) improves the planning modifier by 1, to a max of a -3 difficulty modifier.<br /> -Execution represents a 'full week of work'.<br /> -It is possible to work on multiple projects a week, or to split between planning and execution; this uses the C20 split-action rules.<br /> -It is possible to have 'one' helper per project, who adds half their dicepool to the roll.<br /> <br /> Every 'project type' has multiple difficulty tiers.<br /> -A simple project is difficulty 6 and requires 5 successes.<br /> -Each grade of project complexity adds +1 difficulty and +5 successes required, up to Difficulty 10 at 25 successes.<br /> <br /> ==Project Types==<br /> =Harvesting Dreamstuff=<br /> There are 'four' tiers of Harvesting: Common Dreamstuff, Uncommon Dreamstuff, Rare Dreamstuff, and Legendary Dreamstuff.<br /> -Harvesting gives 5, 4, 3, or 2 volumes at the end of a project, respectively.<br /> -Common Dreamstuff can be used for crafting. Alternately, it can be converted to Dross at a 2-to-1 ratio. Dross can be converted into Common Dreamstuff at a 2-to-1 ratio. Thus, 4 volumes of chimerical stone could become 1 volume of chimerical wood.<br /> -Uncommon Dreamstuff adds 1 chimerical point to a crafting project, which can be distributed among Glamour or Redes.<br /> -Rare Dreamstuff adds 2 chimerical points to a crafting project, which can be distributed among attributes, abilities, glamour or redes. (This is how you can get 'semi-animate' items like dancing swords, etc)<br /> -Legendary Dreamstuff is used to craft a Treasure.<br /> <br /> The planning roll is Perception+Kenning at Difficulty 7, representing 'surveying' an area for the material in question.<br /> The harvesting roll is a Dexterity+Kenning roll, which can be modified by plans and tools.<br /> <br /> =Crafting=<br /> As per the C20 Core Rules.<br /> -An item requires '3' volumes of Dreamstuff per 'moving part'. Thus a dagger requires 3 volumes of Dreamstuff, Scissors require 6 units of Dreamstuff, and crossbow (stock, bow and trigger) requires 9.<br /> -An 'item' may be temporary, whether as a Wonder or as Alchemical Compounds. In this case, the Dreamstuff used to craft it counts as 'one tier higher' for crafting purposes. A Wonder has a number of uses = 6-the level of the Art in question, while a 'potion-of-Rede' recipe creates a number of batches=6-the Glamour/level of the potions in question.<br /> <br /> =Other types of Project=<br /> Hacking, Political Agendas, Oathcrafting or more. It's 'in the same framework' so to speak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25625-magicjuggler","name":"MagicJuggler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25625_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T04:18:42-07:00","id":1407111,"title":"","content":"Hmm interesting! I am in favor of Dreamstuff rankings from Common to Legendary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T11:25:33-07:00","id":1407163,"title":"","content":"Yup. The idea was to create a distinction between &quot;basic chimerical items,&quot; ones with proper redes (as well as a means to mimic stuff from the C20 PG), and Treasures. The only real &quot;exception&quot; to this may be the desire to combowombo rare dreamstuff and legendary in the attempt to design a Glamour Pact monstrosity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25625-magicjuggler","name":"MagicJuggler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25625_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}